Objective
Help establish and grow a sustainable roleplay and social community within Aion 2 while improving player engagement, onboarding, and long-term retention.
Responsibilities
• Developed recruitment strategies and outreach campaigns to attract new community members.
• Organized players into groups based on shared interests, including roleplay activities, dungeon content, raids, and other cooperative gameplay experiences.
• Assisted new and returning players in understanding game systems, progression mechanics, and available content.
• Provided guidance on character development, gameplay optimization, and navigating the limitations of current game systems.
• Helped create opportunities for player interaction through events, group activities, and community-driven initiatives.
• Facilitated communication between community members to support collaboration and positive social experiences.
Key Lessons Learned
Building a successful community requires more than attracting players. Long-term retention is influenced by:

- Effective onboarding
- Clear communication
- Accessible content
- Shared goals
- Social connections
- Meaningful participation opportunities
Through community management and player support activities, I gained practical experience observing how social systems influence player engagement and retention.
